WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.225
Why does identity matter so much now?

2
00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:06.475
Because federal Zero Trust policy
moved where access gets decided.

3
00:00:06.475 --> 00:00:12.041
M-22-09 requires enterprise-managed
identities and phishing-resistant MFA.

4
00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:17.756
NIST 800-207 removes the trust that
used to come from being on the network:

5
00:00:17.756 --> 00:00:20.088
every request is evaluated on its own.

6
00:00:20.088 --> 00:00:24.775
And CISA's maturity model puts
identity first among its five pillars.

7
00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:29.062
In practice, the identity provider
enforces whatever it believes.

8
00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.737
Who is this person,
and is that still true?

9
00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:34.526
Which groups and roles
do they hold, and why?

10
00:00:34.526 --> 00:00:36.525
Is their device managed and healthy?

11
00:00:36.525 --> 00:00:40.329
Conditional Access, Privileged
Identity Management and

12
00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:43.975
device compliance all read
those facts, on every sign-in.

13
00:00:43.975 --> 00:00:45.589
So if the facts are wrong,

14
00:00:45.589 --> 00:00:49.300
every policy built on them is
wrong too, at machine speed.

15
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.340
That's why this move decides whether every
later control has true facts to act on.
